  "body": "Add myself to the Acknowledgments. My earlier pull requests did not include the line the contributing guidelines ask for.\n\nPull requests:\n\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12653 handles processing instruction tokens in the \"in head noscript\" and \"in template\" insertion modes.\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12654 serializes processing instructions with a closing `?>`, so data ending in `?` is preserved when the output is parsed again.\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12658 removes the statement that the insertion mode decides whether CDATA sections are supported.\n\nIssues, comments and reviews:\n\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12023 proposed dropping the distinction between missing and empty DOCTYPE identifiers, which led to https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12084 and Gecko bug https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2010245.\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9559: a test case, `<nobr><table><marquee></table><nobr>`, on which Chrome and Firefox build different trees. https://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/9f50934d44024efb11e276945aca31c4341f3277 clarified the step three days later, and Lexbor fixed its implementation.\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4016 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8558: showed that the standard already specifies CDATA handling at integration points and that browsers differ. WebKit changed to match the standard in https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/69464, which cites the issue.\n- https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4015: proposed stating that foreign content is not an insertion mode, added in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12700 added.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13236/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 8:03 AM UTC (690acd1)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13236/83578e6...690acd1/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 8:03 AM UTC (690acd1)\">diff</a> )",
